     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.75, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.80, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"This is a solid triage with good operational recommendations and appropriate severity calibration. The analyst correctly identified that the account lockout control prevented successful compromise, justifying the medium severity despite multiple failed attempts. The ATT&CK citations are well-chosen (T1110, T1110.001, T1078) and reasonably justified by the brute force attack scenario. For improvement: (1) The confidence score of 0.3 seems inconsistent with the firm conclusion about an external attacker\u2014either raise confidence to 0.6-0.7 or explain what doubts remain; (2) explicitly state why impossible_travel, MFA fatigue, and privilege escalation were assessed as False rather than leaving them blank; (3) consider adding analysis of the failed login pattern (5 attempts in what timeframe?) and whether this aligns with typical brute force tooling versus human error; (4) cite specific LDAP log review findings or recommend checking for password spray patterns across multiple accounts. These additions would move this from good to excellent triage.\"}",
